# M15: a Repository command reaches the folder's own client, and the answer comes back in a window
# of this program's own. The working copies here are ones Git itself made, because Git is the client
# this machine runs; what the other four tools are asked is pinned by the scenarios of src/repo and
# stays unmeasured here, exactly as the README records.

open $T/repo

# Check for modifications answers with the client's own words, and its status line names the call.
select-none
action win.repo.check-modifications
wait-repo-answer M one.txt
wait-repo-answer ?? untracked.txt
expect-repo-status git status --porcelain — done
close-repo

# Commit is asked for its message first — the words its client would otherwise read from an editor —
# and it ran without a word of its own to complain about.
select one.txt
text a message the window asked for
action win.repo.commit
wait-repo-done
expect-repo-status git commit -m a message the window asked for -- one.txt — done
close-repo

# A rename asks for the new name with the old one already in the field; refusing that ask starts no
# client at all, and no answer window opens.
select one.txt
action win.repo.rename
wait-dialog Rename in the repository
expect-dialog-entry Rename in the repository = one.txt
dialog-button Rename in the repository : Cancel
wait-no-dialog Rename in the repository
wait-row one.txt

# A refusal quotes the client's own sentence and names the code it stopped with.
text no-such-branch-here
action win.repo.switch-checkout
wait-repo-answer invalid reference: no-such-branch-here
expect-repo-status refused, exit code 128
close-repo

# Delete and add to ignore list hands the name to the tool's own ignore record, which is a file Git
# reads.
select notes.txt
action win.repo.delete-ignore
wait-repo-answer notes.txt is in .gitignore.
wait-file-text $T/repo/.gitignore = notes.txt
wait-missing $T/repo/notes.txt
close-repo

# Clone is what a folder no tool owns offers, and it asks which address, which folder and which tool
# before anything runs: the folder is the name the address ends with, and the tool named is the tool
# asked.
open $T/plain
action win.repo.clone
wait-dialog Clone a repository
clone-set address = $T/origin
expect-clone-folder origin
expect-clone-tool Git
clone-set tool = Mercurial
expect-clone-tool Mercurial
dialog-button Clone a repository : Clone
wait-repo-answer hg could not be started
close-repo

open $T/plain
action win.repo.clone
wait-dialog Clone a repository
clone-set address = $T/origin
dialog-button Clone a repository : Clone
wait-repo-answer Cloning into
expect-repo-status git clone
expect-repo-status — done
wait-exists $T/plain/origin/.git
wait-row origin
